FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] src/repl/highlight.rs:91 — `runs()` returns plain only for `line.contains('\n')`, but `src/lexer.rs:482` treats lone `\r` as `Newline`, so a CR-only or `\r`-embedded line is still coloured; no test feeds `\n` or `\r` despite REPORT claiming both return plain by that guard — new branch with no test on either side — fix with `line.contains(['\n', '\r'])` and tests for both shapes.
2. [MAJOR] src/repl/editor.rs:734 — `edge_a_piped_session_emits_no_escape_codes_even_with_colour_forced_on` assumes stdin is non-terminal under `cargo test`; with terminal stdin `line_source` returns `EditSource` and `highlights()` is true, so the test is env-coupled — fix by asserting on `PlainSource.highlights()` directly or injecting terminal detection instead of reading the harness stdin.
3. [MAJOR] src/repl/highlight.rs:551 — wall-clock asserts `spent < Duration::from_millis(500)` (and `spent < Duration::from_secs(1)` at src/repl/highlight.rs:589) make the gate machine-dependent; a slow or loaded runner fails despite correct code — fix by asserting round-trip and linearity structurally without wall-clock, or moving timing to a benchmark-only gate.
4. [MINOR] src/repl/highlight.rs:140 — `whitespace[end - 1]` is direct indexing, contradicting REPORT's edge matrix claiming no indexing at all and every position bounds-checked with `Vec::get(..)?` — guarded today only because columns are character columns, but misdescribed and uncovered — fix with `.get()` or correct the matrix.
